## Copied verbatim

- `tools/job_key.py` - canonical dedupe keys for postings
- `tools/page_decode.py` - charset-aware decoding of saved pages
- `tools/robots_check.py` - robots.txt gate (RFC 9309, fail-closed)
- `tools/fetch_page.py` - browser-header GET retry (GET-only, robots-enforced, bounded)
- `tools/posting_guard.py` - integrity gate for untrusted posting text
- `tailor/tools/posting_guard.py` - copied verbatim from ai-job-search
  tools/posting_guard.py (posting integrity gate, tailor's own copy)
- `tailor/tools/page_decode.py` - copied verbatim from ai-job-search
  tools/page_decode.py (dependency of posting_guard.py, tailor's own copy)

## Adapted

- `tools/alert_state.py` - from `tools/scrape_state.py` (dedupe candidates /
  atomic store), rebased on alert-email ingest (URL-only candidates)
- `tools/rank_state.py` - from `tools/rank_state.py` (ranking state machine),
  rebased on the jobseek layout and the Director/VP rubric (seniority gate,
  engineering-role flag, 1-10 score, one-line reason)
- `profile/candidate-profile.md` - from
  `.claude/skills/job-application-assistant/01-candidate-profile.md` (template structure)
- `profile/job-evaluation.md` - from
  `.claude/skills/job-application-assistant/04-job-evaluation.md` (gates,
  weighted dimensions, verdict bands), specialized for Director/VP AI strategy
- `profile/writing-style.md` - from
  `.claude/skills/job-application-assistant/03-writing-style.md` (never-invent
  discipline, tone rules)
- `.claude/agents/posting-scorer.md` - from `.claude/agents/posting-scorer.md`
  (read-only scoring agent pattern), minus the portal-CLI escalation
- `.claude/commands/run-alerts.md` - from `.claude/commands/rank.md` (batch
  scoring flow, trust rules, state-through-tools rule), with Gmail alert
  ingest replacing the portal scrape
- `tailor/tailor.md` - adapted from ai-job-search .claude/commands/apply.md
  (drafter-reviewer workflow, never-invent standing rule, grounding audit,
  ATS keyword check, relevance-weighted cutting; LaTeX compile loop replaced
  by Markdown + pandoc export, cover letter replaced by the 3-line "why me"
  outreach note)
- `tailor/agents/resume-reviewer.md` - adapted from ai-job-search
  .claude/agents/application-reviewer.md (read-only reviewer subagent)
- `tailor/tailor.md` and `tailor/README.md` also incorporate guidance text
  from ai-job-search .claude/skills/job-application-assistant/
  03-writing-style.md, 05-cv-templates.md and 08-application-forms.md
- `tailor/tools/latex_templates/resume.tex.tmpl` - reimplemented from
  ai-job-search's moderncv CV template (no local copy of the upstream file
  was available to vendor verbatim in this environment; structure and intent
  - moderncv `classic` style, name/address/contact header, section-per-block
  layout - follow the upstream template)
- `tailor/tools/latex_templates/cover.cls` - reimplemented from
  ai-job-search's `cover.cls` why-me/cover-letter class, same reason as above
- `tailor/tools/render_latex.py` - new renderer (Markdown -> the templates
  above) written for jobseek's own resume Markdown shape, replacing
  ai-job-search's own LaTeX-authoring convention
- `tailor/tools/compile_latex.py`, `tailor/tools/verify_pdf.py`,
  `tailor/tools/verify_layout.py` - reimplemented from ai-job-search's
  compile-and-inspect loop and its `verify_pdf.py`/`verify_layout.py`
  (page count, ATS text-layer presence, layout overflow/holes), adapted to
  jobseek's export-tool exit-code conventions (0/1/2, matching
  `export_resume.py`)
- `tailor/tools/latex_pipeline.py` - new orchestrator tying the four files
  above into the render/compile/verify/re-render loop; not present as a
  single file upstream
- `tools/notion_sync.py`, `tools/notion_client.py`,
  `.claude/commands/notion-sync.md` - reimplemented from ai-job-search's
  `/notion-sync` command (one-way sync of the tracker/shortlist into a
  Notion database), rebased on jobseek's state/seen_jobs.json schema and
  Director/VP rank fields, and on OAuth-based Notion MCP access (no stored
  Notion API token) instead of ai-job-search's own auth approach

The portal CLIs in ai-job-search derive from Mikkel Krogholm's skills repo
(acknowledged in its README); none of them are copied here.

